                    {
                        "translation_id": "d886401e-2717-4f69-aa6c-ba69a9be1d76",
                        "source_entry_id": "949359e8-7955-3245-82c6-cb753407bace",
                        "source_sense_id": "51840f64-98f5-3146-937a-11d2eefba580",
                        "source_sense_description": "leeres Gerede, Nichtssagendes, aber trotzdem oft eine anspruchsvoll klingende Äußerung",
                        "target_lang_word": "twaddle",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "twaddle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3dc42ba8-dcb4-3d9b-9c3e-888b9c6b4950",
                                        "entry_id": "29704ed7-2ab5-36ea-b81a-037408cd321b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Empty or silly idle talk or writing; nonsense, rubbish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04c6d97c-9ef2-4685-aad9-136266240963",
                                                "sense_id": "3dc42ba8-dcb4-3d9b-9c3e-888b9c6b4950",
                                                "text": "You're talking a load of twaddle. Get your facts straight, man!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca87bb01-20fb-41b1-8a3e-77539214a92c",
                                                "sense_id": "3dc42ba8-dcb4-3d9b-9c3e-888b9c6b4950",
                                                "text": "\"What ineffable twaddle!\" I cried, slapping the magazine down on the table; \"I never read such rubbish in my life.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6dd98eb-0953-479f-9298-ae517b816273",
                                                "sense_id": "3dc42ba8-dcb4-3d9b-9c3e-888b9c6b4950",
                                                "text": "I would rather be rude than to listen to twaddle from a man I’ve known."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f834bbe0-13d3-489d-bef1-0d2aba51677f",
                                                "sense_id": "3dc42ba8-dcb4-3d9b-9c3e-888b9c6b4950",
                                                "text": "It was her other self who had written that letter. It not only bored, it rather disgusted her real self. \"Flippant and silly,\" said her real self. Yet she knew that she'd send it and she'd always write that kind of twaddle to Nan Pym."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12949f06-1ab1-4bc4-87c1-99fcf75c6a8c",
                                                "sense_id": "3dc42ba8-dcb4-3d9b-9c3e-888b9c6b4950",
                                                "text": "I improvised for three or four minutes, speaking complete twaddle in character."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "85ca7b9f-92b1-38c8-bfbc-df1bbe47b3aa",
                                        "entry_id": "29704ed7-2ab5-36ea-b81a-037408cd321b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who twaddles; a twaddler."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "twaddle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "342e586c-4a0f-3ca2-9c86-2f0601a1275f",
                                        "entry_id": "8b75e73d-354c-3d2b-b86b-71cae2344415",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To talk or write nonsense; to prattle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4ff4a32-5ae8-425a-bfef-b30f4fed617e",
                                                "sense_id": "342e586c-4a0f-3ca2-9c86-2f0601a1275f",
                                                "text": "To Edward […] he was terrible, nerve-inflaming, poisonously asphyxiating. He sat rocking himself in the late Mr. Churchill's swing chair, smoking and twaddling."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b6d333de-5dcc-42b9-8742-89a5fc362327",
                        "source_entry_id": "949359e8-7955-3245-82c6-cb753407bace",
                        "source_sense_id": "51840f64-98f5-3146-937a-11d2eefba580",
                        "source_sense_description": "leeres Gerede, Nichtssagendes, aber trotzdem oft eine anspruchsvoll klingende Äußerung",
                        "target_lang_word": "hot air",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hot air",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "81c06405-fb8e-31d4-9021-8149d711b61d",
                                        "entry_id": "802d1f57-2145-320b-a429-8e76000eccc3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Air that has been heated, especially so as to function as the lifting agent of a hot-air balloon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b4cdece-8ea3-4c4a-9729-a29d995f1693",
                                                "sense_id": "81c06405-fb8e-31d4-9021-8149d711b61d",
                                                "text": "The balloon was equipped with a burner to create hot air for lift."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1b9f13a2-c2c5-3cdb-95c7-d6c013e0a165",
                                        "entry_id": "802d1f57-2145-320b-a429-8e76000eccc3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Empty, confused, or exaggerated talk lacking meaning or substance; bluster."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1ecb473-5897-46a7-94a9-daae3271381a",
                                                "sense_id": "1b9f13a2-c2c5-3cdb-95c7-d6c013e0a165",
                                                "text": "\"You'll never get anywhere so long as youse trail with that reform bunch. It's all hot air and tomfool theory.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ab041ea-81bb-4bd2-a2dc-69710879ffed",
                                                "sense_id": "1b9f13a2-c2c5-3cdb-95c7-d6c013e0a165",
                                                "text": "\"You give me a lot of hot air about your conscience. Why don't you get a soap-box and preach on the street-corners?\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd8d4850-a04e-415c-8883-95d97b121129",
                                                "sense_id": "1b9f13a2-c2c5-3cdb-95c7-d6c013e0a165",
                                                "text": "Some of the steam in Washington rises from real issues, but a lot is the hot air of partisan politics."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c3b8117-d98f-4648-b175-6c3a1c08d8e3",
                                                "sense_id": "1b9f13a2-c2c5-3cdb-95c7-d6c013e0a165",
                                                "text": "Klein diagnoses impressively what hasn’t worked. No more claptrap about fracked gas as a bridge to renewables. Enough already of the international summit meetings that produce sirocco-quality hot air, and nonbinding agreements that bind us all to more emissions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e3f0536-2eed-4902-a8e5-0456e51db269",
                                                "sense_id": "1b9f13a2-c2c5-3cdb-95c7-d6c013e0a165",
                                                "text": "I'm afraid I must disagree with Sir Michael Holden, for whom I have enormous respect, when he wrote in RAIL 977 that Transport Secretary Mark Harper's keynote speech for the George Bradshaw lecture in February was \"a breath of fresh air\". More like hot air to me, given Harper's emphasis on the private sector through both a kind of renewed franchising model and open access."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b50ab809-bd3c-48fc-a5e0-5a3107bb86b7",
                        "source_entry_id": "949359e8-7955-3245-82c6-cb753407bace",
                        "source_sense_id": "51840f64-98f5-3146-937a-11d2eefba580",
                        "source_sense_description": "leeres Gerede, Nichtssagendes, aber trotzdem oft eine anspruchsvoll klingende Äußerung",
                        "target_lang_word": "blabla",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "blabla",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cca734d5-4bac-3c3e-8358-492bafd5c4ec",
                                        "entry_id": "aed5edc3-63d0-3a37-b1f1-7fe7f16119ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Flux de paroles inutiles ou incohérentes, discours creux."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "familiar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d348e8a-78d1-401d-ac09-9edf0856eb2c",
                                                "sense_id": "cca734d5-4bac-3c3e-8358-492bafd5c4ec",
                                                "text": "Mais avant cette heure de blabla très intéressante, Jacob avait appelé le président du comité de hand."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50ca148d-8b14-498f-af71-c9b2797a37e1",
                                                "sense_id": "cca734d5-4bac-3c3e-8358-492bafd5c4ec",
                                                "text": "C'est un gang d'hypocrites ! Menteurs un jour, menteurs toujours ! Ils changeront jamais. Tout le temps des cachettes, des belles explications pour se justifier, du blabla, du blabla... pas autre chose que du blabla."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef1d472a-0430-481b-83d9-45c2dca14f54",
                                                "sense_id": "cca734d5-4bac-3c3e-8358-492bafd5c4ec",
                                                "text": "A posteriori, en vue des entretiens, j’ai reconstruit un fil conducteur dans mon orientation, pour garder la face devant les recruteurs. Mais, en vrai, c’est du blabla."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a45ee9e-8dbf-4d60-9f93-06b3929af0aa",
                                                "sense_id": "cca734d5-4bac-3c3e-8358-492bafd5c4ec",
                                                "text": "Et enfin, je n’aime pas tout ce blabla sur les possibilités de devenir un athlète pro, quand on a huit fois plus de chances de faire une chute mortelle dans sa baignoire (véridique !)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
